## Context

Child of 1654. The round-one citation collection exists on the unmerged branch `t1654-citation-chaining` (archive root `data/rel_chaining/2026-10-08/`; merged pool of 597,494 works built 2026-10-09 on dedup version 1, baseline 389,291). This ticket lands the collector and the round-one delivery, and archives the merge. It does not screen anything: the staged screening is retired (ticket 2062) and new works are scored by the redesign (ticket 2060, then 2063).

Sequencing: finish and archive on dedup version 1 before the version-2 flip (ticket 2048 stage B2b), or the flip must carry a migration for the chaining records.

## Exit criteria

- [x] Counts for round one, from the archive: references and citations retrieved, duplicates, genuinely new works, unresolved references; the arithmetic shown.
- [x] The collector lands as a lane (`scripts/_rel_chaining.py`, `scripts/catalog_rel_citation_chaining.py`, `tests/test_rel_citation_chaining.py`, a short doc); the screening-only code (`scripts/corpus_rel_chaining_screen.py`, `tests/test_rel_chaining_screen.py`) does not land; diff at most 14 content-bearing paths.
- [x] The round-one delivery is under the intake contract with provenance, pushed to DVC as immutable, and the pool merge rebuilt from it reproduces the archived merge (hashes quoted).
- [x] Records are left unscored; no label is created or changed by this ticket.
- [x] Scoped gate quoted (`selected:` and `skipped:`).
